.TH cadcraft-cli 1  "cadcraft-cli 0.18.0 (32238e83c2c8bf643994132883e94bc96961f649)" 
.SH NAME
cadcraft\-cli \- cadcraft\-cli: headless CADCraft
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBcadcraft\-cli\fR [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fB\-V\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR] <\fIsubcommands\fR>
.SH DESCRIPTION
cadcraft\-cli: headless CADCraft
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
cadcraft\-cli\-info(1)
Print a drawing\*(Aqs summary as JSON
.TP
cadcraft\-cli\-convert(1)
Convert a drawing; OUT\*(Aqs extension picks the format (dxf, dwg, dwt, svg, png, pdf)
.TP
cadcraft\-cli\-run(1)
Open drawings (or start a new one), run scripts and commands in order, save or export the result
.TP
cadcraft\-cli\-commands(1)
Print the command catalog as JSON
.TP
cadcraft\-cli\-mcp(1)
Run the MCP server on stdio: a headless drawing session, or a bridge to the running app
.TP
cadcraft\-cli\-perf(1)
Time the engine on a synthetic N\-entity drawing (default 200000), or the canvas display\-list build of a drawing, zoomed in step by step
.TP
cadcraft\-cli\-sample(1)
Write a built\-in sample drawing
.TP
cadcraft\-cli\-roundtrip(1)
Open each DXF/DWG, save it as DXF and DWG, reopen and compare; writes report.md and report.json
.SH VERSION
v0.18.0 (32238e83c2c8bf643994132883e94bc96961f649)
